1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,560
In this tutorial, you'll learn how to modify an intercepted request in BERT proxy.

2
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:16,700
This enables you to manipulate the request in ways that the website isn't expecting

3
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,780
in order to see how it responds.

4
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:23,960
Using one of our deliberately vulnerable websites, known as Labs, you'll see how this can help

5
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:27,780
you identify and exploit real vulnerabilities.

6
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:31,580
To follow along, you'll need an account on portswigger.net.

7
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:35,400
If you don't have one already, registration is free and it grants you full access to the

8
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,460
Web Security Academy.

9
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:44,980
In BERT, go to the Proxy Intercept tab and make sure Intercept is switched off.

10
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:50,860
Launch BERT's browser and use it to visit the following lab.

11
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:56,760
The lab is entitled, Excessive Trust in Client Side Controls.

12
00:00:56,760 --> 00:01:00,080
When the page loads, click Access the lab.

13
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:04,260
If prompted, log into your portswigger.net account.

14
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:09,820
After a few seconds, you'll see your own instance of a fake shopping website.

15
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:15,140
On the shopping website, click My Account and log in using the following credentials.

16
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:19,160
Username, Winer, password, Peter.

17
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:26,900
You can check these out on the accompanying tutorial on our website.

18
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:36,900
When you log into the account, notice that you have just $100 of store credit.

19
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:40,220
Click Home to go back to the home page.

20
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:46,200
Select the option to view the product details for a lightweight leather jacket.

21
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:51,560
In BERT, go to the Proxy Intercept tab and switch Interception On.

22
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:56,260
In the browser, add the leather jacket to your cart to intercept the resulting post forward

23
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:59,200
slash cart request.

24
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,620
You may initially see a different request on the Proxy Intercept tab if the browser is doing

25
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,780
something else in the background.

26
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:11,100
In this case, just click forward until you see the post request generated when you click

27
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:15,980
the Add Cart button.

28
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:21,080
Study the intercept request and notice that there is a parameter in the body called price, which

29
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:29,860
matches the price of the item in cents.

30
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:34,260
Click into this parameter and change the value to 1.

31
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:41,040
Then click forward to send the modified request to the server.

32
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:47,640
Switch Interception off again so that any subsequent requests can pass through BERT proxy uninterrupted.

33
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:54,360
In BERT's browser, click the basket icon in the upper right corner to view your cart.

34
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:58,480
Notice that the jacket has been added for just one cent.

35
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:01,360
There is no way to modify the price via the web interface.

36
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:06,500
You were only able to make this change thanks to BERT proxy.

37
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:11,320
Click the place order button to purchase the jacket for an extremely reasonable price.

38
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:15,720
Congratulations, you've just sold your first Web Security Academy lab.

39
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:22,720
You've also learned how to intercept, review, and manipulate HTTP traffic using BERT proxy.

40
